# Code owners for the two acts by people. A template: copy these lines into .github/CODEOWNERS of the repository
# where the studies live, and put the platform logins or teams of the people who may make each act in place of
# the names in capitals. With "Require review from Code Owners" switched on for the protected branch, a pull
# request that touches one of these paths cannot be merged without an approval from one of the people named.
#
# A lock: the scientist who asked and the steward of the knowledge the study belongs to.
studies/*/lock-request/          @THE-STEWARD @THE-SCIENTIST
# A signature: the steward, and nobody else.
studies/*/signature-request/     @THE-STEWARD
# What the acts rest on. A change to any of these is reviewed by the same people, in a pull request of its own:
# the required check refuses a pull request that carries a request and also changes one of them.
/tools/                          @THE-STEWARD
/factory/                        @THE-STEWARD
/.github/                        @THE-STEWARD
